<title>USA: Innovex up after stock split.</title>
<headline>Innovex up after stock split.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Innovex Inc shares were up 2-1/4 at 39-1/4 on Wednesday after the company announced a two-for-one stock split today.</p>
<p>Don Eller, director of research at H.J. Meyers &amp; Co, said the stock split will improve liquidity in the shares. Fundamentals at Innovex remain strong, he added.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Innovex reported record earnings for fiscal 1996 of $1.81 a share after a $0.05 charge, compared with year-ago results of $1.40.</p>
<p>Innovex makes precision electrical components for the computer electronics and medical instruments markets.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
